{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013FZvu6eBN7fp4SZJbek7Sf","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# metadata-forensics — technique log (days 1-8; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- Every day = ONE evidence zip (`metadata-day-NN-evidence.zip`, plain Deflate, no password so far). Days 1-7: one tiny\n7\t  member (33 B - 3 KB) and ONE structural fact. Day 8: the zip carried the whole cumulative kit (note + jpg + png + pdf +\n8\t  inner zip, 3.3 KB) and even the SINGLE contract asked all 12 fields (identity + every earlier day's field + the new one).\n9\t  The member can itself be a container (Day 7/8: an inner ZIP whose own EOCD / central directory is the asked field).\n10\t- A new `<fmt>.<field>` family each day: identity (name/size/hashes) -> magic prefix -> `text.utf8_bom_present` ->\n11\t  `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` -> `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` -> `pdf.header_version` -> `zip.eocd_total_entries` ->\n12\t  `zip.central_directory_member_names`. Since Day 3 the question literally names the field (`Determine <fmt>.<field> for\n13\t  <member>`); answer ids read `dNN-<fmt>-NNN-<fmt>-<field>` (`.`/`_` -> `-`). NOTE the `dNN` is the drop/member family,\n14\t  not the day the field appeared: Day 8's new field came as `d07-zip-001-zip-central-directory-member-names`.\n15\t- The prompt's flavor text describes decoys (impostors, renamed copies, \"-with-bom\" names, EXIF/presentation lies, chunk\n16\t  \"passengers\", catalog /Version overrides, \"impossible provenance\" names). The asked field so far was always the\n17\t  STRUCTURAL truth from the header/record bytes; names/extensions/secondary metadata are the lie. All 8 single solves were\n18\t  first-submit CORRECT in ~27-60 s; every TT/Mastery since Homebase (D4+) CORRECT first try.\n19\t- Titles are puns, not format hints: Day 7 \"Seven-Zip, No Relation\" was plain ZIP (PKWARE), no .7z anywhere.\n20\t\n21\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants -- parse every value listed)\n22\t- **Delivery layout** -- see \"Delivery layouts seen\" below; resolve the named member through whatever wrapper arrives.\n23\t- **Decoys** -- renamed copies, misleading extensions/names, secondary metadata (EXIF, catalog /Version) that disagree\n24\t  with the header: always answer from the structural header bytes of the member the question names.\n25\t- **Member and values** -- names, sizes, dimensions and counts re-roll per variant; nothing about the sample is\n26\t  constant (Day 7 entry count went 2/3/4/5 with drop number 001-004; member names `room-NN/item-K.txt`). Day 8 re-rolled\n27\t  ONLY the note's case id (`Case <hex> evidence note.`, 33 B) -> md5/sha1/sha256/magic differ per set; jpg 257x146, png\n28\t  269x153, pdf 1.4, eocd 2, CD names identical across single/TT/5 Mastery sets. Never cache a value across sets anyway.\n29\t- **ESCALATED field set** -- the contract grows over time: D7 TT/Mastery went 1 -> 11 fields (Mastery 22); D8 started at\n30\t  12 already in single (TT 12, Mastery 5 sets x 12 = 60). Families: the day's field +\n31\t  `evidence-note-{filename,size-bytes,md5,sha1,sha256,magic-prefix-hex-16,text-utf8-bom-present}` + carry-overs\n32\t  `d04-jpeg-*-sof-dimensions-pixels`, `d05-png-*-ihdr-dimensions-pixels`, `d06-pdf-*-header-version`, `d07-zip-*-eocd-\n33\t  total-entries`, `d07-zip-*-central-directory-member-names`. Dispatch on the answer-id SUFFIX and keep EVERY earlier\n34\t  family answerable (reference: `challenges/day08/metadata-whats-in-the-box/solver/solve.py` answers all 12).\n35\t- **Answer kinds** -- `exact_text`, `integer`, `pattern` (hashes, case-insensitive), `enum` (`accepted_values`), and\n36\t  since D8 `json` (\"compact valid JSON array with exact values and order\"). Emit per `answer_format.kind`.\n37\t- **Nesting depth** -- the asked file may sit 2-3 zips deep (Mastery D7: outer -> `...-evidence-0N.zip` ->\n38\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); resolve by the name after `->`, never answer from an enclosing zip.\n39\t\n40\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n41\t| You see | First move |\n42\t|---|---|\n43\t| `<zip> -> <member>` in `questions[].artifact` | `7z l -slt <zip>` then `7z x -o work/ <zip>`; (or python `zipfile` read of the member) |\n44\t| filename / size / md5 / sha1 / sha256 | `stat -c %s`, `md5sum sha1sum sha256sum` on the extracted member (bytes, not the zip entry name) |\n45\t| \"first sixteen bytes\", \"magic\", \"extension claims\" | `xxd -p -l 16 <member>` (lowercase, no spaces); `file -k` only for orientation |\n46\t| `text.*_bom_present` | `xxd -l 4`: UTF-8 BOM = `ef bb bf` (UTF-16LE `ff fe`, BE `fe ff`, UTF-32LE `ff fe 00 00`) -> `true`/`false` |\n47\t| `jpeg.*dimensions*` / SOF | walk JPEG segments from `ffd8` by length to SOFn (`ffc0..ffcf` minus c4/c8/cc): P, Y=height, X=width. `exiftool -ImageSize` cross-check only |\n48\t| `png.ihdr_*` / \"walk their chunks\" | `xxd -s 16 -l 8` = IHDR width,height (BE u32). Chunk walk = len/type/data/CRC loop (`lib.stego.png_chunks`) |\n49\t| `zip.eocd_*` / \"count what the archives claim\" | of the NAMED inner zip (not the evidence zip): last `PK\\x05\\x06` whose comment len reaches EOF; u16 @+8 disk entries, @+10 total, u32 @+12 cd size, @+16 cd offset, u16 @+20 comment len. `0xFFFF` -> ZIP64 locator `PK\\x06\\x07` (EOCD-20) -> `PK\\x06\\x06` u64 @+32. Cross-check: count `PK\\x01\\x02` walking from cd offset, `PK\\x03\\x04` |\n50\t| `zip.central_directory_*` / \"inventory every stored path, preserve directory context\" | walk `PK\\x01\\x02` from EOCD cd-offset (fallback `EOCD - cd_size` if data prepended): name len u16 @+28, extra @+30, comment @+32, name at +46; next = +46+n+e+c. Raw stored path, CD order, no basename/dedupe/sort; decode UTF-8 (flag bit 11 `0x800`, else try UTF-8 then cp437). `7z l -slt` / `zipinfo -1` as cross-check |\n51\t| `pdf.header_version` / \"declared versions\" | `head -c 16 <f> | xxd` -> `%PDF-x.y` at offset 0; `grep -a -o '/Version[^/>]*'` only as a diagnostic |\n52\t| \"impostor\", \"renamed\", \"disguise\" | trust magic bytes at offset 0; a matching string deeper in the file is a decoy |\n53\t| answer_format syntax \"use the literal none only when the requested field is absent\" | field missing (e.g. no header) -> `none` |\n54\t| answer_format kind `json` | `json.dumps(v, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)` -- compact, no spaces, no Markdown |\n55\t| Mastery `set1.`..`setN.` ids, artifact `delivery N: <zip> -> <member>` or `<zip>-0N.zip -> <member>` | resolve each set's member separately; see delivery layouts below |\n56\t\n57\t## Day by day\n58\t**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity inventory). Zip with one text member (prompt says \"three files\";\n59\tonly one present in single; TT used `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed `evidence-note-copy.txt` + original).\n60\t- Asked: filename (base name with extension), size-bytes (integer), md5, sha1, sha256 (hex, case ignored).\n61\t- Worker: python `zipfile` + `hashlib`; submitted at step 4, CORRECT ~36 s after launch, first try.\n62\t- Mastery layout first seen: ONE download named after set1's zip, containing BOTH per-set zips (zip-of-zips).\n63\t\n64\t**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (magic prefix vs extension). Field `<member>-magic-prefix-hex-16`.\n65\t- Answer = first 16 bytes of the member, lowercase hex, 32 chars, no `0x`/spaces. Single member was honest text.\n66\t- Variants: TT `readme.exe` that was actually UTF-8 text; Mastery set2 `disguised-report.bin` that was a PDF.\n67\t- TT quirk: contract question text named `roster.csv` while `answer_ids` said `readme-executable-...` and the zip held\n68\t  only `readme.exe` -> fix was `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted` (match member to answer-id stem, exe~executable). Always\n69\t  answer under `answer_ids`, trust the zip contents.\n70\t- TT submits all came back `expired` (5 s window, harness latency, pre-Homebase) — not an analysis error.\n71\t- Mastery zip-of-zips broke name lookup (outer zip has set1's name but not the member) -> returned the inner zip's\n72\t  `PK..` bytes. Fix: `find_artifact` recurses nested zips (depth 4), prefers member whose parent zip is the named one.\n73\t- Single CORRECT in ~34 s.\n74\t\n75\t**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (text encoding). `text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`.\n76\t- Read first 3 bytes for `EF BB BF`; single member started `Case` -> false. CORRECT ~28 s, first try.\n77\t- Mastery set2 member named `export-001-with-bom.txt`: decide from bytes, never the name (that one did have a BOM).\n78\t- Solver also covers utf16/utf32 `_bom_present` variants (unconfirmed spellings).\n79\t\n80\t**Day 4 — Picture This** (JPEG). `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` exact_text.\n81\t- Walk segments by declared length (no fixed offsets) to the SOFn frame header; one SOF0 at 0x88; P=8, H, W.\n82\t- GM-confirmed form `<width>x<height>` (X first, lowercase x, no spaces). Not EXIF/filename dims.\n83\t- Prompt hinted rotation/\"presentation vs structure\" mismatch — not asked; solver carries best-effort exif_orientation /\n84\t  display dims (unconfirmed). CORRECT ~38 s. TT/Mastery CORRECT in-window (solve phase 0.12 s of a 6 s window).\n85\t\n86\t**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (PNG). `png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels` exact_text.\n87\t- IHDR at offset 0x10: BE u32 width, height -> `<width>x<height>` (same form as Day 4, applied by analogy, accepted).\n88\t- Verified geometry: inflated IDAT length == H*(1+W*bpp); chunks IHDR/IDAT/IEND, CRCs ok, no trailing data (the\n89\t  \"structural passenger\" = extra chunk / data after IEND, not in the asked file). Tools: `7z x`, `xxd`, `dd`.\n90\t- CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n91\t\n92\t**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (PDF). `pdf.header_version` exact_text.\n93\t- `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> answer bare `x.y`. Only one `%PDF-` marker; no catalog `/Version`; exiftool PDFVersion agreed.\n94\t- Rules adopted: header must be at file start (BOM/whitespace prefix tolerated); `%PDF-` deeper in the file (decoy in an\n95\t  impostor) is NOT the header -> `none`; catalog `/Version` (PDF 32000 §7.2.2, incl. incremental updates) never changes\n96\t  header_version. The impostor/`none` and override cases are synthetic (built by the worker), NOT GM-judged yet.\n97\t- Mastery delivery changed: two downloads with the SAME filename, saved/addressed as `delivery 1: <zip>` /\n98\t  `delivery 2: <zip>`; artifact field `delivery N: metadata-day-06-evidence.zip -> document-00N.pdf`.\n99\t- Pre-fetched mastery contract.json listed document-003/004; the live attempt asked 006/007 -> read the live start.\n100\t- CORRECT ~34 s; TT in_window 2.7 s (GM start call itself took 23 s that day — latency is outside the window).\n101\t\n102\t**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (ZIP EOCD census). `zip.eocd_total_entries` integer, id `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`.\n103\t- Evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip` (410 B, Stored, data-descriptor flag) with `room-01/item-1.txt`,\n104\t  `room-02/item-1.txt` (identical 48 B text). EOCD total-entries u16 @+10 = 2 -> answer `2` (base-10, no units).\n105\t- All variants were honest: EOCD disk/total == CD headers == LFHs, no comment/trailing bytes. The prompt's \"empty space\"\n106\t  / \"census that does not add up\" (claim vs real walk, padding, dir entries) was flavor only — not exercised, so it is\n107\t  still unknown whether the GM wants the claimed or the walked count when they differ. Answer the field = the CLAIM.\n108\t- Worker: `xxd | tail` + `7z l -slt` on triage's pre-extracted inner zip, then stdlib `struct` EOCD parser in solve.py\n109\t  (ZIP64 aware). CORRECT 57 s after start, first try. TT 3 entries (in_window 0.89 s / 7 s); Mastery set1 4, set2 5\n110\t  (1.33 s / 7 s). Pre-fetched mastery contract (003/004) matched live this time.\n111\t\n112\t**Day 8 — What's in the Box?** (`zip.central_directory_member_names`, kind `json`, id\n113\t`d07-zip-001-zip-central-directory-member-names`). Prompt: \"The count was only the beginning. Inventory every stored\n114\tpath, preserve directory context, and identify the archive whose names reveal an impossible provenance claim.\"\n115\t- Artifact: 3308 B evidence zip with 5 members (`evidence-note.txt` 33 B, `camera-001.jpg`, `panel-001.png`,\n116\t  `document-001.pdf`, and the SAME 410 B `evidence-drop-001.zip` as Day 7). Single contract = 12 fields at once.\n117\t- Key insight: the field = the inner zip's central-directory filename fields, verbatim and in CD order:\n118\t  `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` -- the two basenames collide, so \"preserve directory context\" means keep\n119\t  the full stored path (never basename/dedupe/sort). No `../`, absolute, backslash or UTF-8/cp437 oddities appeared in\n120\t  any variant (UT extra, 2026-10-01 09:00, unix attrs); the \"impossible provenance\" decoy was NOT exercised -- still answer\n121\t  the raw CD names (the field says central_directory, not LFH, not sanitized).\n122\t- Worker: 3 tool calls -- read contract + Day 7 solver, `7z l -slt` + `xxd | tail` on the pre-extracted inner zip, then\n123\t  copied the Day 7 solve.py and added a CD walker + `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"), ensure_ascii=False)`.\n124\t  Start 15:43:55Z -> CORRECT 15:44:22Z (~27 s), first try, all 12 confirmed.\n125\t- TT: 8 s window, in_window 1.15 s (solve 0.13 s), CORRECT. Mastery: 5 sets / 60 answers, 10 s window, in_window 1.34 s,\n126\t  CORRECT. Only the note's case id differed between variants.\n127\t- LIB (ratchet D8): spelling recorded as `knowledge.ZIP_CD_MEMBER_NAMES_FMT` -> `json.dumps(names, separators=(\",\",\":\"))`.\n128\t\n129\t## GM answer conventions learned\n130\t- Filenames: exact base name incl. extension, no directory. Sizes: base-10 integer, no units. Hashes: hex, case ignored.\n131\t- Byte prefixes: lowercase hex, contiguous, exactly 2N chars (`xxd -p -l N`).\n132\t- Booleans: enum `true` / `false` (lowercase) — the contract hands the vocabulary; pick, don't probe.\n133\t- Pixel dimensions (JPEG SOF, PNG IHDR): `<width>x<height>` — width first, lowercase `x`, no spaces (GM-confirmed both,\n134\t  re-confirmed D8 `257x146` / `269x153`).\n135\t- PDF header version: bare `x.y` from the leading `%PDF-x.y` (no `PDF-`/`%` prefix); absent header -> literal `none`\n136\t  (contract wording; `none` itself not yet GM-confirmed).\n137\t- Counts (`zip.eocd_total_entries`): plain base-10 integer string, e.g. `2` (GM-confirmed D7 + D8 all modes).\n138\t- JSON lists (`zip.central_directory_member_names`): compact array, no spaces after `,`, double quotes, full stored path\n139\t  with `/` dirs, CD order -- `[\"room-01/item-1.txt\",\"room-02/item-1.txt\"]` (GM-confirmed D8 single/TT/Mastery x5).\n140\t  Whether the GM's `trim` normalization also tolerates `\", \"` spacing is untested -- always emit compact.\n141\t- Rejected spellings: none recorded in this lane (no wrong submission in any mode, days 1-8).\n142\t- `knowledge.py`: `JPEG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PNG_DIMENSIONS_FMT`, `PDF_HEADER_VERSION_FMT`, `ZIP_EOCD_TOTAL_ENTRIES_FMT`, `BOOL`.\n143\t- Inference: the field id IS the spec name (`sof_dimensions_pixels` = SOF frame header, `ihdr_` = IHDR chunk,\n144\t  `header_version` = file header, `eocd_total_entries` = EOCD record's own claim, `central_directory_member_names` = CD\n145\t  file-name fields) — read the field name literally to pick which structure to parse; a claimed count is NOT a CD walk /\n146\t  `zipfile` len, and CD names are NOT local-header names (they happened to agree on D7/D8).\n147\t\n148\t## Delivery layouts seen (resolve these before parsing)\n149\t- Single / TT: one zip; members named in `artifact` after `->` (D8: 5 members, filename question's artifact = zip only).\n150\t- Mastery days 1,2,4,5: ONE download named `...-evidence-01.zip` that is an outer zip containing `...-01.zip` and\n151\t  `...-02.zip` (zip-of-zips); each inner zip holds its set's member.\n152\t- Mastery day 7: zip-of-zips again, three levels (outer `-01.zip` holds `-01.zip` + `-02.zip`, each holding the asked\n153\t  `evidence-drop-00N.zip`); artifact ref `metadata-day-07-evidence-0N.zip -> evidence-drop-00N.zip` (no `delivery N:`).\n154\t- Mastery day 8: same shape, FIVE sets: one 17 KB download `metadata-day-08-evidence-01.zip` (Stored, UTF-8 flag) holding\n155\t  `-01.zip`..`-05.zip`, each a full 5-member kit (incl. its own `evidence-drop-001.zip`). Refs `...-evidence-0N.zip ->\n156\t  <member>`; every set reuses the same member names, so resolve by (set zip, member), never member name alone.\n157\t- Mastery day 6: two downloads with identical filenames -> `delivery 1: <zip>` / `delivery 2: <zip>` in artifact refs.\n158\t- Member numbering shifts between pre-fetched contract and live attempt (003/004 vs 006/007) — never hardcode names.\n159\t\n160\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n161\t- Name lookup by zip filename alone breaks on zip-of-zips (returned `PK` bytes as the \"magic\") — recurse into nested zips.\n162\t- Contract question text can be stale vs `answer_ids` (Day 2 TT): answer under `answer_ids`, locate the member that exists.\n163\t- Don't let the flavor text widen the question: prompts mention impostors/passengers/orientation/provenance, but only the\n164\t  named field is graded. Answer it; keep extra checks as diagnostics.\n165\t- Container-of-containers: when the asked file is itself a zip, a naive `rfind(PK\\x05\\x06)` on the downloaded evidence\n166\t  zip reads the OUTER EOCD / CD (D8 outer CD = the 5 kit members, Mastery outer = 5 set zips). Resolve the named member's\n167\t  bytes first, then parse.\n168\t- Name-list fields: `zipfile.namelist()` is CD order but decodes non-UTF-8-flagged names as cp437 and is fine for honest\n169\t  zips; for hostile names (`../`, `/abs`, `C:\\`, `\\` separators, LFH != CD name, duplicates) emit the CD bytes as-is --\n170\t  don't let an extractor's sanitizing (7z/unzip strip `../` and leading `/`) rewrite the answer.\n171\t- Decoys by name: `*-with-bom.txt`, `.exe` that is text, `.bin` that is PDF, `.pdf` that is PNG — bytes win every time.\n172\t- Timed windows are ~5-10 s (D8: TT 8 s, Mastery 10 s for 60 answers) and most of it is GM start/download/submit\n173\t  round-trips (solve ~0.1-0.2 s): never do anything slow (extraction to disk, exiftool) in-window; parse in memory.\n174\t- Fastest path for a new carry-over day: copy the previous day's solver (which already answers every earlier family) and\n175\t  add only the new suffix handler -- D8 went start -> CORRECT in 27 s that way.\n176\t- Harness: re-running `hctf start` on an already-solved challenge overwrote `single_solve/start.json` and made the stop gate\n177\t  think it was incomplete (Day 2, ~2 min lost) — restore start.json from `log.jsonl`.\n178\t- Tools installed (2026-10-07): exiftool, pdfinfo/pdftotext (poppler), qpdf, mutool, pdf-parser, pdfid, pngcheck,\n179\t  zsteg, steghide, binwalk, foremost, mediainfo, sqlite3, identify/convert (ImageMagick), olevba/oleid.\n180\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015GTSiXQiFz2SK1f3Jnj6gx","agent_id":"aacda09a92d161c5d","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"50ef2066-548a-44ac-af2f-1c1a819224c3","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:02:57.913Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_013FZvu6eBN7fp4SZJbek7Sf","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"metadata day09 technique log"}
