{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01W4TNER59FzaaXbAQXxeSrC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# script-analysis — technique log (days 1-8; updated after every day)\n2\t\n3\tHow this lane has looked so far (these are observations, not guarantees):\n4\t- **Timed variants MUTATE** (organizer, Day 8: \"new, dynamic variations/mutations ... new unseen effects\"): nothing below is a\n5\t  guarantee for Time Trial / Mastery -- solvers derive structure and degrade per field.\n6\t- There is one AES zip, `evidence.zip` (password `infected`), of inert \"Huntress Script Triage\" fixtures. **The contract is CUMULATIVE.** Each day keeps every earlier language's files and questions and adds ONE new host language or host format. The bytes and values re-roll every day:\n7\t  PS (d1, 15 ids) -> +JScript (d2, 87) -> +Batch (d3, 159) -> +VBScript (d4, 231) -> +Python (d5, 357) -> +Bash (d6, 399)\n8\t  -> +Node.js `.mjs` and 2 Bash advanced-syntax fixtures (d7, 469) -> +8 PHP \"polyglot\" files, 4 WSF/HTA/PHP-webshell \"host\"\n9\t  files and 2 more Bash advanced fixtures (d8, 615). The title names the new language; the prompt names its NEW roles.\n10\t- From day 2 on, every fixture hides a **self-describing plan**: `v=N|steps=a,b|adapter=..|stage_count=..|campaign_id=..|<indicators>`. It sits behind a codec, usually named in a `Codec_<id>` / `CODEC_<id>` / `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` const of the form `rep|transform|key`. Most exact_text answers are plan values copied verbatim.\n11\t  From D8 there is also a **`v=3` plan**: it carries `role=` and `attack=` itself, and sits behind a `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` comment.\n12\t- The hard part is **naming CODE SHAPE**: control-flow, expansion, and function/invocation/property styles. These are GM synthetic labels that are not in the plan. Role and scenario are enums, so read `accepted_values`.\n13\t- Files are named by behaviour (host-context, memory-stage, embedded-write, remote-write, local-dispatch, staged-handoff/-chain, outbound-transfer, impact-plan, relay-handoff, schedule-descriptor). The answer-id is `<lang>-<role>-<field>`, and the artifact path picks the file. Don't trust the file name over the plan `steps`.\n14\t- Time Trial windows are about 5-13 s (30 s on d1). Mastery has `setN.` ids: 2 sets on d2-d7, **5 sets / 3075 ids / 22 s on d8**.\n15\t  The artifact was `evidence-0N.zip`, or (d6) `delivery N: evidence.zip`, or (d7-d8) ONE download `evidence-01.zip` that holds\n16\t  every `evidence-0N.zip`. Same-named deliveries: pair them by sha256.\n17\t\n18\t## Variant axes (what differs between the single, Time Trial and Mastery variants of the SAME day -- parse every value listed)\n19\tEach miss below cost one failed timed attempt + a ~45-90 s generalize cycle (D6 replay: 4 cycles; D7: 1 cycle; D8: 0).\n20\t- **Codec per file** -- rep x transform x key re-rolls per variant; never bind a role to the sample's codec. **NEW rep\n21\t  NAMES appear only on variants** (D7 TT: `unicode_escapes` `\\u00XX..`, `json_numbers` `[232,241,..]`,\n22\t  `reversed_base64`, Bash `xor_hex|cd`). Decode by the material's SHAPE (escapes / int array / hex / base64, each also\n23\t  reversed) x the named transform, and accept only output starting `v=`; the name only orders the tries.\n24\t- **Codec spec arity** -- 3 fields `rep|transform|key`, 2 fields `rep|` (empty transform = identity; D7 bash advanced\n25\t  fixtures), or the transform folded into the rep with the key second (`xor_hex|cd`, D8 `xor_hex|11`, `xor_hex|d8`).\n26\t  Split on `|`, never index blindly. lib.codec (`_spec`) normalises both short forms; every D7/D8 codec rep decodes in lib.codec.\n27\t- **Plan carrier tag (v=3, D8)** -- `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-<data>`, plus the same data in `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"`.\n28\t  Values: `B64` (base64), `HEX` (plain hex), `HB64` (hex of base64 text = 2 layers), `FRAG` (hex split by `.` every 24 chars).\n29\t  Across single + TT + 5 Mastery sets the tag stayed fixed per file; only the values re-rolled. Parse rule: ignore the tag\n30\t  name. Peel by shape and recurse (max 3 layers): if the text is only hex digits plus `.:,-_ |\\x%` separators, strip the\n31\t  separators and unhex; otherwise base64 (also reversed). Accept only a result starting `v=`. The tag = `obfuscation_profile`.\n32\t  LIB (ratchet D8): `lib.codec.find_codecs(src)` now returns the v=3 plan (tag -> rep: B64 base64_literal, HEX/FRAG\n33\t  hex_compact, HB64 new rep `hex_base64`), 84/84 D8 fixtures; ATT&CK = plan's `attack=` (`knowledge.V3_ROLE_ATTACK_CONFIRMED`).\n34\t- **Numeric literal radix** -- the same array/constant may be decimal `23,7`, hex `0x17,0x07`, or a separator-joined\n35\t  string decoded with `parseInt(x, R)` / `int(x, R)`: READ THE RADIX FROM THE CODE, never guess it from the digits\n36\t  (D6: JScript material array hex on TT; decoder constants `^ 0x56`; Mastery dash-joined DECIMALS with\n37\t  `parseInt(..,10)`). Applies to keys too.\n38\t- **Base64 alphabet** -- standard and urlsafe (`-` `_`) both occur; strip/whitelist accordingly and pad (D6 Python TT).\n39\t- **Reversal level** -- `reversed_hex/_decimal/_integer_list` reverse the loaded LIST; `reversed_base64` reverses the\n40\t  TEXT before decoding (`==Adu..`). Try both orders.\n41\t- **Carrier of the same language** -- plain source vs a frozen executable (D6: Python plan inside a cx_Freeze build on\n42\t  a TT variant). Locate the material by its markers (`MATERIAL_`/`CODEC_`/`v=`/`HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_`), not by file type.\n43\t- **Material layout** -- one literal, split chunks, `+=` concatenation, adjacent quoted strings, `.`-separated FRAG\n44\t  fragments; join before decoding.\n45\t- **Adapter values** re-roll within a role (Node stager http_then_module/https_then_vm/fetch_then_function; launcher\n46\t  execfile_node/fork_module/spawn_file; persistence systemd_descriptor/npm_lifecycle_descriptor) -- always plan-verbatim.\n47\t- **D8 cases** auto-time_trial-129bf46a, auto-mastery-07d5051a (5 sets): no new axis. Values re-rolled; structure, tags,\n48\t  role/attack/steps/profiles were identical to the single solve. Both were CORRECT on the first try.\n49\t\n50\t## Recognition cues -> first move\n51\t| You see | First move |\n52\t|---|---|\n53\t| `evidence.zip`, \"method=AES Encrypted\" | Already extracted by triage (`work/extracted/`, password `infected`) and every plan decoded in triage.md -- start from that, BUT diff the extracted member list against the contract's `artifact` names. Triage silently skipped new extensions: D7 `.mjs` (no decode lines) and D8 `.php` (0 of 8 decoded; HB64 peeled only 1 layer). In solve.py open members with `lib.common.read_member` (Python zipfile cannot read AES). Mastery may be a zip inside a zip; walk it once. |\n54\t| Prior-day languages in the contract | Cumulative: derive every family from TODAY's bytes with the shared codec method below (never copy/run an old solver). Spend thinking on the new language. |\n55\t| `.ps1` with `$encodedMaterial = [Convert]::FromBase64String('..')` + `$reconstruct` + `$nativeTypes` | `base64 -d` -> JSON descriptor (short keys a/b/c..): url/wallet/mutex/UA/file/ext/note. Match indicators by SHAPE, not key. `$nativeTypes` gives the scenario: Process/Registry+wallet=resource, ZipFile/HttpWebRequest=collection, Aes/DirectoryInfo=impact. |\n56\t| `.js` WSH, `decode_*`/`recover_*`/`inspect_*`, XOR key arrays, `\"52:90:..\"` strings | Run each file in an empty `node` `vm` context (no require/ActiveXObject), `eval` swapped for a capture. Call the top-level functions and keep the first object that has `steps`. Read the styles off the `inspect_*` body. |\n57\t| `.bat/.cmd` with `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:` / `HUNTRESS-MATERIAL:`, `set \"itemN=v=1|steps=..`, `:HUNTRESS_INSPECT` | Plan is in plain `set` fragments. Emulate cmd expansion in Python (`%v%`, `!v!`, `call set %%..%%`, `for %%G in (..)`). The MATERIAL line is a 2nd encoded copy to cross-check. Never run cmd. |\n58\t| `.vbs` with `Const Material_<id>`, `Const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, `Load_/Decode_/Recover_<id>` | Decode in Python from the Codec const, cross-check against the Load/Decode code (no cscript). rep/transform answers = Codec fields 1/2 verbatim. Control = the construct wrapping the `Decode_` call inside `Recover_`. |\n59\t| `.py` `*-recovered.py` with `MATERIAL_<id>`, `CODEC_<id>`, `load_/decode_/surface_/plan_<id>` | Already-recovered source (no decompile on d5). Decode from CODEC or run `decode_(load_(MATERIAL))` under an AST whitelist. Plan v=2 carries syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain verbatim. |\n60\t| `.sh` `readonly Material_<id>='..'` + `readonly Codec_<id>='rep|transform|key'` | Decode from the Codec const (key hex; multi-byte key = COMMA list). Re-join split/`+=`/adjacent-quoted chunks. Never run bash. |\n61\t| `.sh` with `Feature_<id>()` (`${!pointer}`, `local -a parts=('cu' 'rl')`, `local -A`, `${arr[@]:1:2}`), plan `v=1|feature=..|primitive=..` | Role `advanced_syntax` (closed enum value). feature/primitive/campaign/stage_count/steps are plan-verbatim; attack = T1059.004. |\n62\t| `.mjs` ESM: `const Material_<id> = \"..\"; const Codec_<id> = \"rep|transform|key\"`, async `load_/decode_/recover_/inspect_/plan_<id>`, `process.env.HUNTRESS_INSPECT_ONLY` | Static decode with `lib.codec.find_codecs` + shape fallback (reps hex_buffer, hex_array, escaped_octets `\\\\xNN`, decimal_array, unicode_escapes, json_numbers). Don't run it (top-level await, Buffer/vm). Plan fields verbatim; role from `steps`. |\n63\t| `// HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<B64|HEX|HB64|FRAG>-..` + `descriptor_<id> = \"..\"` (`.php` `declare(strict_types=1)`; `.js` that is really HTA `<html><hta:application>` or a WSF `<job><script language=\"JScript\">`; `.vbs` that is a WSF job mixing VBScript+JScript) | **Route by the marker, before the extension** (the extension lies). Peel the descriptor by shape to `v=3|language=..|role=..|attack=..|adapter=..|host_profile=..|obfuscation_profile=..|stage_profile=..|next_language=..|stage_count=..|steps=..|campaign_id=..|url=..|file_path=..`. EVERY answer, including role and attack, is plan-verbatim. Python `-I` + base64/bytes.fromhex is enough. |\n64\t| Real `.pyc` / PyInstaller / pyarmor (not seen yet) | `lib.pyc.recover_python(path)` (pyinstxtractor-ng + decompyle3, `dis` fallback). See skills/script-analysis. |\n65\t| Any `Codec_` key like `ba` / `0a` | A hex byte, not text. Transforms are named for the ENCODE side: `subtract_modulo_256` decodes by ADDING, `add_modulo_256` by SUBTRACTING. `rolling_xor` = c ^ previous CIPHER byte, seeded with the key. |\n66\t\n67\t## Codec table (`Codec_<id>='<rep>|<transform>|<key>'`, batch `rem HUNTRESS-CODEC:<rep>|<transform>`; seen D3-D8)\n68\t**Already done for you:** triage.md's \"Decoded payloads\" runs `lib.codec` on every declared codec (and a node vm\n69\tsandbox on JScript). In solve.py call `lib.codec.find_codecs(text)` / `lib.codec.decode(material, rep, transform, key)`\n70\t(pure Python, Homebase-safe, unknown names -> None). A line `NOT decoded by lib.codec` = new rep/transform/arity: decode\n71\tit by material shape yourself and list it under `## Proposed lib additions` in NOTES.md.\n72\t- Reps (how the bytes are WRITTEN): base64_literal/_chunks, urlsafe_base64, reversed_base64 (D7); hex_pairs/_compact/\n73\t  _colon/_dash/_escape (`\\x`)/_literal (`0x`)/_buffer/_array (`[\"69\",\"22\"]`), percent_hex (`%xx`), escaped_octets\n74\t  (`\\\\xNN`), unicode_escapes (`\\\\u00NN`); decimal_bytes/_comma/_dash/_pipe/_dot/_colon/_space/_csv/_array, json_numbers,\n75\t  integer_list/_tuple, octal_space; reversed_text/_hex/_decimal/_integer_list; plain_fragments/split_fragments.\n76\t- Transforms (ENCODE-side names; key hex, multi-byte = COMMA list): identity (also EMPTY field), reverse/reverse_bytes,\n77\t  single_byte_xor, repeating_key_xor, reverse_then_xor, rolling_xor (2 flavours), add_modulo_256 (decode SUBTRACTS),\n78\t  subtract_modulo_256 (decode ADDS); batch carries the parameter in the name: xor_5a, add_7 (decimal), rotate_left\n79\t  (undo = rotate right), reverse_xor; bash D7 `xor_hex|cd` = hex then XOR key cd.\n80\t- Check: the decoded plaintext starts `v=` (or `{` JSON). If not, the codec reading is wrong.\n81\t\n82\t## Day by day\n83\t**D1 Power Play (PS, 15 ids)**: 3 PS fixtures, base64 JSON descriptors. Collection ATT&CK cost 5 wrong (T1005, T1560,\n84\tT1119, T1074, T1074.001) before `T1555.003` -- tell was `Login Data`/`Cookies`. **Map the SPECIFIC artifact, not the\n85\tgeneric tactic.** ~15 min.\n86\t\n87\t**D2 Host With the Most (+9 JScript, 87)**: plans behind base64/XOR arrays/reverse/byte-shift, eval'd by `inspect_*`;\n88\tnode `vm` + eval capture. Handoff graph = `staged_chain` even with a .js next_stage (`relay` REJECTED). 7 wrong, all\n89\tATT&CK guesses (see table). ~22 min.\n90\t\n91\t**D3 Expansion Pack (+9 Batch, 159): the costly day, ~1 h 45 min, ~127 rejected probes.** expansion/control are GM\n92\tlabels, not surface reading; `if defined X` burned ~40 synonyms before `if_guard`. -> NAMING LAWS. `%item0%` is a\n93\tvariable, not `%0`.\n94\t\n95\t**D4 Dim and Dimmer (+9 VBScript, 231)**: Codec const + small VBS-subset interpreter. Control probed one field at a\n96\ttime (direct/select_case/do_once/while_once; TT added error_guard/for_once). 4 wrong, ~7 min.\n97\t\n98\t**D5 Hatch Careful (+14 Python \"carriers\", 357)**: prompt promised pyc/PyInstaller/pyarmor but the zip held\n99\t`*-recovered.py` source; plan v=2 gave every label verbatim. 0 wrong, ~4 min. `dispatch_next_stage` = relay.\n100\t\n101\t**D6 Shell We Begin (+6 Bash, 399)**: Material/Codec/Load/Decode/Recover with noise wrappers. New fields stage-count\n102\t(= plan stage_count, NOT len(steps)) and steps (`>`-joined). 399/399 first submit, ~4 min.\n103\t\n104\t**D7 Node by Node (+8 Node.js `.mjs` + 2 Bash advanced-syntax, 469 ids)**: prompt \"Eight Node.js operation graphs\n105\tthat will never execute. Spot the indirect expansions and token fragmentation, then sort each graph into its role\".\n106\t- Artifact: one AES `evidence.zip`, 61 members (D6 set + `node-*.mjs` + `indirect-expansion.sh`/`token-fragmentation.sh`).\n107\t- Node files = same Material_/Codec_ pattern as VBS/Bash, in ESM JS. Static decode via lib.codec + shape fallback;\n108\t  answers plan-verbatim. Fields: role, attack, adapter, campaign, <indicator>, stage-count, steps.\n109\t- New roles: `build_schedule>register_descriptor` = `persistence_descriptor` -> **T1053.003** (by ROLE: adapter was\n110\t  systemd_descriptor / npm_lifecycle_descriptor, schedule_path `/etc/cron.d/node-xxxxxx`). Bash fixtures with plan\n111\t  `feature=` (steps recognize_syntax>reconstruct_intent, stage_count 1) = `advanced_syntax` -> T1059.004; feature\n112\t  indirect_expansion|token_fragmentation, primitive parameter_indirection|array_token_construction.\n113\t- New indicator keys (plan-verbatim): schedule_path, service_name (`node-xxxxxx.service`, on staged_chain).\n114\t- 469/469 first submit, ~100 s (D6 solver copied + Node/advanced branch; triage had no `.mjs` decodes).\n115\t- TT (11 s window): attempt 5ab8013f missed 15 ids -- new reps unicode_escapes/json_numbers/`xor_hex|cd`; harvested\n116\t  variant 7d6f8d53 added `reversed_base64|`. Attempt 26b7da83 got a 24 B `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` saved as\n117\t  evidence.zip. 3rd attempt 516aa6d1 CORRECT (9.5 s in-window: start 3.9 + download 3.1 + submit 6.0). Mastery\n118\t  2c52d50f (13 s) CORRECT first try, 3.9 s in-window; 938 ids, one bundle holding evidence-01.zip + evidence-02.zip.\n119\t- NOTES.md's \"VARIANT AXIS: none\" came from the 2nd generalize worker, which looked only at the rate-limited attempt.\n120\t  The real axis was the new reps found by the 1st worker. **Diagnose EVERY failed attempt, not only the latest.**\n121\t\n122\t**D8 Lost in Translation (+8 PHP polyglot, +4 host-format, +2 Bash advanced; 615 ids)**: prompt: \"The same indicators show\n123\tup in every language the campaign speaks, each with its own quoting, escaping, and encoding accent. Normalize them ...\n124\tfind the one that doesn't match its siblings\". No question asked for an outlier; the prompt is flavour.\n125\t- Artifact: AES `evidence.zip` with 75 members, the D7 set plus:\n126\t  - `polyglot-php-<role>.php` (8 roles);\n127\t  - `host-wsf-jscript-jscript.js`, `host-wsf-mixed-vbscript.vbs` (WSF job markup), `host-hta-jscript-javascript.js`\n128\t    (HTA HTML), `host-php-webshell-php.php`;\n129\t  - `associative-arrays.sh`, `array-slicing.sh` (`local -A`, `${values[@]:1:2}`; feature associative_arrays|array_slicing,\n130\t    primitive declare_associative|indexed_array_slice).\n131\t- Key insight: the new files carry a `v=3` plan behind `HUNTRESS_ANALYSIS_V1:<TAG>-` + `descriptor_<id>`. The comment and\n132\t  the descriptor were byte-identical in every file of all 7 deliveries. The plan states role/attack/adapter/profiles itself,\n133\t  so **copy it, do not derive it**. v=3 steps do NOT predict role (an uploader had `decode_configuration,return_configuration`;\n134\t  a launcher had `acquire_remote,dispatch_process`).\n135\t- New fields (all plan-verbatim):\n136\t  - host-profile: standalone | wsf_jscript | wsf_mixed | hta_jscript | php_webshell\n137\t  - obfuscation (= `obfuscation_profile`): base64 | plain_hex | hex_base64 | fragmented_hex\n138\t  - stage-profile: single_descriptor | two_stage_download_execute | three_stage_decode_write_launch | cross_language_handoff\n139\t  - next-language: powershell/jscript/javascript/vbscript/batch/python/bash/php\n140\t  - The adapters were abstract: local_parser, runtime_loader, file_writer, http_client, process_builder, schedule_builder,\n141\t    operation_graph.\n142\t- Method: copy D7 solver, add a v=3 branch that runs BEFORE extension routing (marker regex; recursive shape peel; plan_kv;\n143\t  `steps` comma->`>`). The worker hand-decoded all 12 descriptors with a 10-line `python3 -I` (B64/HEX/HB64/FRAG) first.\n144\t- Time: start 15:43:58 -> submit 609/615 accepted 15:45:26 -> CORRECT 15:46:07 (**~2 min 10 s, 2 submits, 0 wrong**).\n145\t  The 6 misses were the new Bash families: ids like `bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature` have hyphenated family\n146\t  names, so the prefix-strip regex left `arrays-feature`. Fix: match the field as the longest known `-<field>` SUFFIX.\n147\t- TT (9 s window) CORRECT 1st try, 2.1 s in-window (start 0.58, download 0.27, solve 1.04, submit 0.8). Mastery (22 s,\n148\t  5 sets, 3075 ids, one bundle with evidence-01..05.zip) CORRECT 1st try, 5.6 s in-window (solve 4.1 s).\n149\t\n150\t## GM answer conventions learned\n151\t- **Check `answer_format.kind` first.** `enum` gives the list (scenario, role). `mitre_attack_id` takes `T####[.###]` or literal `none` (benign_utility). `integer`/`ordered_tokens` (d6+). `exact_text` = plan value or synthetic label.\n152\t- **Plan-verbatim fields** (copy exactly):\n153\t  - adapter: COM ProgIDs `MSXML2.ServerXMLHTTP.6.0`, LOLBins `CertReq.exe`, batch `call`/`set`/`for`, Node\n154\t    `console_report`/`typed_array_to_file`/`stream_pipeline`, D8 `http_client`/`operation_graph`.\n155\t  - indicators: campaign_id, host_id, url, file_path, upload_url, next_stage, extension, note_name, handoff_id, cron_path,\n156\t    schedule_path, service_name. Indicator questions read \"exact X indicator\", where X is the plan key.\n157\t  - per-language labels: batch `graph`, Python syntax/obfuscation/carrier/windows_chain, Bash feature/primitive,\n158\t    D8 v=3 host_profile/obfuscation_profile/stage_profile/next_language.\n159\t  - **v=3 role and attack too.** GM accepted the plan's PARENT technique ids: `T1059` (launcher, staged_chain) and `T1053`\n160\t    (persistence_descriptor), NOT the host-language sub-technique. The role->ATT&CK table below is for v=1/v=2 plans only.\n161\t- **Role from `steps`** (v=1/v=2 plans; v=3 states `role=`):\n162\t\n163\t  | steps | role |\n164\t  |---|---|\n165\t  | decode_configuration,return_configuration | benign_utility |\n166\t  | acquire_remote + dispatch_memory/dispatch_pipe | stager |\n167\t  | acquire_remote,write_file | downloader |\n168\t  | decode_embedded,write_file | dropper |\n169\t  | locate_local,dispatch_process | launcher |\n170\t  | read_file/upload,transmit_remote | uploader |\n171\t  | transform + recovery_note | impact |\n172\t  | build_schedule,register_descriptor (Node d7) | persistence_descriptor |\n173\t  | recognize_syntax,reconstruct_intent + plan `feature=` (Bash d7-d8) | advanced_syntax |\n174\t  | ends in handoff_script (JS/Batch/VBS) or profile_host..dispatch_process | staged_chain |\n175\t  | dispatch_next_stage (Python) | relay |\n176\t\n177\t  cron_path/service_name on a staged_chain are indicators only, NOT persistence.\n178\t- **Role -> ATT&CK** (GM-confirmed d2-d7; `lib.scripts.role_attack(role, lang)` has the table):\n179\t  - benign `none`; downloader and stager T1105; dropper T1140; uploader T1041; impact T1486; persistence_descriptor\n180\t    T1053.003 (by role, whatever the adapter); advanced_syntax T1059.004.\n181\t  - launcher/staged_chain/relay follow the HOST LANGUAGE: T1059.003 batch, .004 bash, .005 VBS, .006 python, .007\n182\t    JScript AND Node.js (.001 PS predicted, never asked).\n183\t  - PS scenarios: resource_hijacking T1496, synthetic_collection T1555.003, synthetic_impact T1486.\n184\t  - REJECTED: T1218.010, T1620, T1027.009, T1005, T1560, T1119, T1074(.001); stager T1059.007; dropper T1105.\n185\t- **Batch expansion** (closed set; mined from EVERY GM-verified D3-D6 case, 0 conflicts in 545):\n186\t  - fragments named `h<N>` AND joined with `call set` (bare, or `for %%G in (..) do call set`) = `call_double`\n187\t  - `for %%G in (..) do call set \"cfg=%%cfg%%%%<pool>%%G%%\"` over any OTHER pool (v_a/item/fragment/FrAg) = `for_indirect`\n188\t  - everything else = `delayed`, INCLUDING h-pools joined with `!h0!!h1!..` (the \"h-pool = call_double\" shortcut failed).\n189\t  - Fragment JOINER pitfall: `set \"item9=%item0%%item1%...\"` is the JOIN, not fragment 9 -- skip `set` lines whose\n190\t    value references the other fragments (a wrong Mastery answer on D6).\n191\t  - REJECTED: percent_expansion, immediate, call-double, double_call.\n192\t- **Batch control**: direct (separator lines and `:HUNTRESS_UNUSED` dead labels are NOT control), errorlevel_guard\n193\t  (`ver >nul` + `if errorlevel 1 exit /b 1`), goto_dispatch, call_subroutine, if_guard (`if defined X`). REJECTED:\n194\t  linear, straight_line, sequential, goto, goto_label, double_pipe, pipe, ampersand, call_label, dead_label, errorlevel,\n195\t  opaque_branch, + ~40 \"if defined\" synonyms.\n196\t- **VBS control**: direct, select_case, do_once, while_once, error_guard (`On Error Resume Next`..`Err.Raise`),\n197\t  for_once. REJECTED: do_loop, do_exit, while_wend, while_loop, on_error_resume.\n198\t- **Codec labels**: representation/transform = the codec const's fields 1/2 copied VERBATIM; spellings differ per\n199\t  language (Python `decimal_csv`, batch `decimal_bytes|reverse_xor`): read the const, never translate.\n200\t- **JScript styles** (closed sets in the question text; GM-confirmed D2-D8):\n201\t  - function-style: `function f(` = declaration; `var f = function(` = anonymous_expression; `var f = function f_body(` = named_expression.\n202\t  - invocation-style: how recover/inspect invokes the next top-level function: `f(x)` = direct, `f.call(..)` (also via\n203\t    a local `invoke` helper doing `block.call`) = call, `f.apply(..)` = apply.\n204\t  - property-style: only `o.k` = dot, only `o[\"k\"]` = bracket_literal, both = mixed. triage's `shape:` line counts them.\n205\t- **NAMING LAWS** (proven on if_guard, error_guard, do_once, pe_cli). Compose unknown labels from the SHORT language keyword:\n206\t  - conditional/bail-out = `<keyword>_guard`; run-once loop = `<keyword>_once`; control transfer = `<keyword>_<action>`.\n207\t  - The spelled-out statement (if_defined, on_error_resume, do_exit, while_wend) and descriptive synonyms (flag_guard, defined_guard, opaque_predicate) have ALWAYS been rejected.\n208\t\n209\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n210\t- **Probing synonyms instead of deriving.** D3 lost ~1.5 h and two fields hit the 6-wrong cap on `if defined`. Apply the naming laws first; `hctf labels` seeds candidates from lib/playbook.py.\n211\t- **Per-set POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the whole batch; `--from-solver` bisects and prints the rejected id(s). Probe uncertain label fields ONE per submit; the wrong cap is per field.\n212\t- **Generic ATT&CK guesses** (d1 collection, d2 launcher/stager/dropper): use the role->ATT&CK table. Adapter names (regsvr32, systemd_descriptor) do NOT change the technique.\n213\t  Exception: a plan that states `attack=` (v=3) is authoritative even when it is a parent id (T1059, T1053).\n214\t- **Routing by file extension** (D8): `.js` held HTA/WSF markup and `.vbs` held a WSF job with VBScript+JScript. The\n215\t  extension-based JS/VBS paths would mis-parse them. Check for the plan marker first; use the extension only as a fallback.\n216\t- **Answer-id field parsing** (D8, 6 ids lost on the 1st submit): new family names contain hyphens\n217\t  (`bash-advanced-associative-arrays-feature`, `polyglot-php-persistence-descriptor-stage-profile`). Resolve the field\n218\t  as the longest known `-<field>` suffix (`stage-count`/`stage-profile` before `stage`), not by a prefix-strip regex.\n219\t- **GM error body saved as the artifact** (D7 TT 26b7da83): `{\"error\":\"rate_limited\"}` (24 B) landed as `evidence.zip`,\n220\t  so every field came out None/default. Before solving/diagnosing, check artifact size + sha256 against the contract\n221\t  `sha256`; a tiny JSON `{\"error\":..}` = transport failure (retry), NOT a variant. Solvers should exit non-zero on it.\n222\t- **Unknown codec rep name -> silent no-plan** (D7 TT: 15 ids unanswered). Fall back to material-shape readings x the\n223\t  named transform; never let an unknown NAME stop the decode.\n224\t- **Batch expansion shortcuts** (\"h-pool = call_double\", \"`%` join = percent\") were wrong. Use the mined rule above.\n225\t- **cmd arg parsing**: `%item0%` is a variable, not `%0`+`item`. CRLF/LF mixes and `SeT` casing occur.\n226\t- **Bash Codec key**: comma-separated multi-byte keys parsed as contiguous hex silently give key [0]. Use `lib.scripts.codec_key()`.\n227\t- **stage_count != len(steps)** (d6). Read the plan field.\n228\t- **Timed modes are a transport race.** D2 Mastery expired (downloads ate 4-5 s of 6 s; sets submitted serially). D7 TT\n229\t  spent 13.5 s for 0.4 s of solving (start 3.9, download 3.1, submit 6.0); D8 transport was fast (start 0.6-1.5 s).\n230\t  Solver ~0.2-4 s (D8 Mastery: 5 sets in 4.1 s); submit all sets in one call.\n231\t- **Same-name deliveries.** Pair Mastery files by sha256; if delivery 2 is missing, leave set 2 unanswered rather than\n232\t  reuse set 1's members (confidently wrong 42-174 times in regression cases).\n233\t- **Re-walking nested AES zips per question** cost ~1.3 s (903 PBKDF2 runs). Index the tree once.\n234\t- **Never execute fixtures.** Every decode so far worked from the Codec const plus a restricted interpreter of the\n235\t  Load/Decode bodies. Cross-check two decoders; accept a plan only if it parses as `k=v|..` with `steps` (or `feature`).\n236\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01D5fvyzqtnx6EA57P5CBGwm","agent_id":"a2acad75aff1f1411","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"856a7332-0573-4b18-aa68-19f6a9186dc7","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:03:18.068Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01W4TNER59FzaaXbAQXxeSrC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"scripting day09 technique log"}
