{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfriBSy4GXpnip3nChTyg","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`. It is now 172 lines, down from 180.\n\n**What Day 9 was:** \"Trust Everyone\", with the mechanic \"permissive X509 trust manager\". The prompt asked to exploit a challenge CA, but the APK had no TLS code or certificate files at all, and the dex class `TrustEveryone` is an empty stub. It was the same 12704 B, 6-entry APK as every earlier day. The answer sat in `assets/huntress_puzzle.json`, encoded as base64 (codec repeated from day 3): `QU5TLTNEM0I4MDM5NTI0MEI4RUU=` -> `ANS-3D3B80395240B8EE`.\n\n**What I added:**\n- **Day 9 entry:** the artifact, the codec, and the worker flow (2 tool calls, `lib.android.decode_payload`, `hctf submit --from-solver`, no decompiling and no chasing the unreachable loopback URL).\n  - Single solve: CORRECT 25 s after start, first try.\n  - Time Trial (8 s window): correct in 3.16 s. 1.99 s of that was the solve phase, probably slow imports on first run, which the entry notes.\n  - Mastery (11 s window, 5 sets): correct in 1.7 s.\n  - No wrong submissions.\n- **Header:** the theme list, the codec-repeat list and the dex marker strings now include day 9, and \"all 8 days\" became 9. The title now says days 1-9.\n- **Variant axes:** merged into the existing axes. Base64 has no key, so the 7 variants differed only in `data`. All Mastery sets shared one loopback slug (`d09-92be5cd6e8a5594f`), and Mastery had 5 sets again. No `VARIANT AXIS:` lines turned up in the challenge folder, and the two auto cases (Time Trial and Mastery) all used base64.\n- **Recognition cues:** a new row for the \"exploit a challenge CA\" prompt: check `unzip -l` for a cert or network config, otherwise decode the asset.\n- **Pitfalls:** the timed-window line now says 6-11 s, and the \"prompt wording escalates, the artifact did not\" pitfall now includes day 9.\n- **GM answer conventions:** `ANS-<16 uppercase hex>` with `exact` normalization was confirmed on 7 of 7 day-9 variants. Mastery used `set1..set5.answer` on days 8-9.\n- To make room, I shortened the Day 1-6 entries.\n\nCANDIDATE LIB ADDITIONS:\n- **(a) Codec:** none needed. The day-9 codec is base64, which `lib/android.py` `_decode_declared` already handles (`codec in (\"base64\",\"b64\")`). The solver only calls `decode_payload(pz[\"codec\"], pz[\"data\"], pz.get(\"key\"), ANS.fullmatch)` plus the existing split, `decode_any` and `extract_answer` fallbacks. The one piece of solver logic that isn't in a lib function is the inline split handling, which tries both readings of `order`. `puzzle_candidates` already does this per the doc, so the next solver should call it instead of copying the snippet.\n- **(b) GM-confirmed facts:** `lib/knowledge.py` and `lib/playbook.py` hold no mobile-android facts. Candidates, backed by `confirmed.json` for days 1-9 with no rejections:\n  - `MOBILE_ANSWER_RE = r\"^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$\"` with `exact` normalization.\n  - Mastery ids are `setN.answer`, with 5 sets on days 8-9.\n  - A playbook rule for this lane: the answer is the decoded `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` value, and the `127.0.0.1:19090` loopback URL (the \"backend\") is never reachable or needed. This has held on all 9 days, and the GM accepted that value as the \"backend answer code\"."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1744,"cache_read_input_tokens":63981,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1744,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01WkGQjyKybr6sFDaHwLXtRR","agent_id":"a9833030737543b64","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"905623a7-632d-4