{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WcT4n3qf8Kuyp58AKRxoZs","type":"tool_result","content":"1:# warmups — technique log (days 1-9; updated after every day)\n7:- The ENCODING changes daily and the title/prompt is a pun naming it: 64 -> base64, \"thirteen steps\"/half a turn -> ROT13, sixteen fingers -> hex, \"two sides\" -> 8-bit binary, \"reduced to numbers\" -> decimal char codes, \"eight fingers\" -> octal, \"address bar\"/\"Percent\" -> URL percent-encoding, \"the browser understands\"/\"Entity\" -> HTML character entities, \"characters would like to escape\"/\"Escape Room\" -> JSON/JS `<BS>uXXXX` string escapes. Every single_solve so far was ONE layer.\n8:- Mastery is cumulative. Day N mastery = 5N-2 sets (3, 8, 13, ..., 38, 43). Each set blob has N numbered lines `NN<TAB>fragment`, and line k uses day k's encoding (b64, rot13, hex, binary, decimal, octal, url-%XX, html-entity, `\"'+U+'XXXX\"`, in that order so far). The last line has no trailing newline. The fragments join verbatim (split mid-word) into the same sentence.\n13:  entities, `\"<BS>uXXXX\"` JSON escapes, ...); detect each line's encoding from its alphabet, not its position (position-based detection breaks if the order\n14:  changes). Rule for \"escape-token\" encodings (url `%xx`, entities): accept when the WHOLE fragment is tokens of that kind\n15:  (`re.sub(token,'',frag).strip()==''`), then use the stdlib decoder (`unquote`, `html.unescape`) so the unseen forms\n17:  Day 9 backslash escapes: every char as lowercase `<BS>u00XX`, the fragment WRAPPED IN DOUBLE QUOTES (a JSON string\n18:  literal) in all 45 blobs (single, TT, 43 mastery lines); no `<BS>x`, `<BS>n`, `<BS>\"`, uppercase hex or non-ASCII seen. Rule: if\n19:  the fragment is `\"?(<BS><BS>[u x n r t \" <BS><BS> /]...)+\"?`, decode with `json.loads` (add the quotes if missing) -- that also covers\n20:  `<BS>n`, `<BS>\"`, surrogate pairs and non-ASCII; fall back to `codecs.decode(t,'unicode_escape')` for `<BS>xNN`. Drop the quotes.\n22:- **Set count** -- grows by 5 per day (33 on day 7, 38 on day 8, 43 on day 9); the solver must loop over whatever the contract lists.\n26:- **Fragment whitespace** -- payload spaces sit at fragment edges (day 9: 34/43 rot13 line-2 fragments end in a space, `pbqvat guvf `). Never `.strip()` the decoded text of a fragment before joining.\n38:| `&#78;&#105;&#99;...` (only `&...;` tokens, no line end) | HTML entities: `python3 -c \"import html,sys;print(html.unescape(open(sys.argv[1]).read()))\" blob.txt` (covers `&#x..;` and named too) |\n39:| `\"<BS>u004e<BS>u0069...\"` (quoted, only `<BS>uXXXX`; prompt says \"escape\") | JSON string escapes: `python3 -c \"import json,sys;print(json.loads(open(sys.argv[1]).read()))\" blob.txt`. `lib.decode.decode_chunk` also gets it (generic fallback, ASCII only) |\n88:- 620-byte blob of decimal HTML entities only (`&#78;&#105;&#99;...`, no line end), ONE layer -> `html.unescape` -> slug.\n90:- A pre-warmed worker made 2 tool calls: `html.unescape` plus a `lib.decode.decode_chunk` cross-check (it also handles entities,\n91:  via its generic fallback), then patched the solver and submitted. Start (15:43:54Z) -> CORRECT (15:44:12Z) about 18 s, first submit.\n92:- Solver: if a fragment is all `&...;` tokens -> `html.unescape`, else `decode_chunk`. TT window 8 s, CORRECT at 2.6 s.\n97:**Day 9: Escape Room** (\"These characters would very much like to escape.\" -- backslash/unicode escape sequences).\n99:  One layer -> `json.loads` -> sentence -> slug. `lib.decode.decode_chunk(text.strip())` already returned the plain sentence\n100:  (its generic `<BS>u/<BS>x` escape fallback keeps only the escapes, so the quotes vanish).\n101:- Pre-warmed worker: 3 tool calls (read triage/contract/skeleton; `decode_chunk` + `json.loads` cross-check; patch `answer()`\n103:- Solver: `decode_chunked` for `NN<TAB>` blobs else `decode_chunk`, then the last-line slug regex. Its `json.loads`\n104:  post-step never fired (lib had already unescaped).\n105:- TT window 7 s, CORRECT at 0.8 s after start (whole run 1.6 s). Mastery 43 sets x 9 lines (+ quoted `<BS>u` line), zip\n106:  bundle as `blob-01.txt`, window 9 s, CORRECT at 0.9 s (solve 0.3 s). Both on attempt 1, 43/43 slugs accepted as decoded.\n107:- Gap: lib's `<BS>u` path is ASCII-only (`_ascii`); a non-ASCII escape (`<BS>u00e9`) makes the whole fragment fall through\n112:- No correctly decoded warmups answer has been rejected (days 1-9; day 8's 40 and day 9's 45 slugs all accepted as decoded). The only `incorrect` (day 7 mastery set1) was a wrong value from decoding the whole bundle. The value is self-describing, so verify it against `answer_format.syntax` and submit.\n126:- Hand-testing escape decoders: in a ratchet session, a literal backslash-u sequence typed into a Bash/heredoc command\n127:  reached python ALREADY decoded (the tool layer unescaped it), so a test \"passed\" on plain text. Test on the artifact file\n128:  or build escapes with `chr(92)+'u%04x'`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_016qGSngjh22hfzcG5yNyPyv","agent_id":"aed02cd9fb3b16140","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"70a7236e-7259-4b7d-a2a6-57b830ddb17d","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:04:51.622Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01WcT4n3qf8Kuyp58AKRxoZs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"warmups day09 technique log"}
