{"type":"system","subtype":"task_notification","task_id":"aed02cd9fb3b16140","run_id":"0mv0z6mc5-ae83b750","tool_use_id":"toolu_016qGSngjh22hfzcG5yNyPyv","status":"completed","output_file":"/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/tmp/claude-1000/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe/tasks/aed02cd9fb3b16140.output","summary":"I added a Day 9 entry to `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/warmups.md` (now 130 lines) and updated the header, variant axes, cues and pitfalls. That file is the only one I changed.\n\n**What day 9 was:** the challenge was \"Escape Room\" (\"These characters would very much like to escape.\"). The 644-byte `blob.txt` is a single quoted JSON string: `\"` + 107×`\\u00XX` (lowercase, every character) + `\"`, with no line end. It is one layer, decoded with `json.loads`. Start to CORRECT took about 30 s (13:00:06Z to 13:00:36Z), with 3 worker tool calls and the first submit correct. Time Trial: 7 s window, CORRECT 0.8 s after start. Mastery: 43 sets × 9 lines, 9 s window, CORRECT at 0.9 s. Both passed on attempt 1.\n\n**Changes to the notes:**\n- **Header:** title now says days 1-9, plus the \"escape\" pun → `\\uXXXX`, the 5N-2 set count reaching 43, and the 9 s Mastery window.\n- **Variant axes:**\n  - Encoding per line: line 9 is a quoted `\"\\uXXXX\"` JSON string in all 45 blobs. The parse rule is regex `^\"?(?:\\\\(?:u[0-9a-fA-F]{4}|x[0-9a-fA-F]{2}|[nrt\"\\\\/]))+\"?$`, then `json.loads` (adding quotes if missing), with `unicode_escape` as the fallback for `\\x`.\n  - Set count: 43. Delivery: days 7-9 all used the same zip bundle. Payload: Single 644 bytes vs Time Trial 650.\n  - New \"Fragment whitespace\" axis: 34 of 43 line-2 (rot13) fragments end in a space, so a decoded fragment must not be stripped before joining.\n- **Recognition cues:** a new row for quoted `\"\\u004e\\u0069...\"` points to `json.loads`.\n- **Pitfalls:** in this session, a literal backslash-u typed into a Bash/heredoc command reached Python already decoded, so a hand test can falsely pass. Test on the artifact file, or build escapes with `chr(92)`.\n\n**Candidate lib additions:**\n\n(a) `\\u` / JSON-string escapes. `lib/decode.py` decodes these only in the `_generic_chunk` fallback, and it is ASCII-only:\n- Sample input from `blob-01.txt` line 9: `\"\\u0065\\u0072\\u002d\\u0072\\u0069\\u0070\\u0070\\u006c\\u0065\\u002d\\u0037\\u0036\"` → `er-ripple-76`. `decode_chunk` does get this right, and `decode_chunked` reproduces both sampled slugs (sets 1 and 2).\n- The gap: I tested `\"\\u0063\\u0061\\u0066\\u0065\\u00e9...\"`, and `decode_chunk` returned rot-N garbage (`\"\\e0063\\e0061...\"`), because `_ascii()` rejects é. `\\n`, `\\\"` and surrogate pairs would also be dropped silently. None of these have appeared in the challenge's bytes yet.\n- Suggested fix: a strict branch in `decode_chunk` before the `good` filter: if `re.fullmatch(r'\"?(?:\\\\(?:u[0-9a-fA-F]{4}|x[0-9a-fA-F]{2}|[nrt\"\\\\/bf]))+\"?', t)`, then take `json.loads(t if t.startswith('\"') else '\"'+t+'\"')`, or `codecs.decode(t.strip('\"'),'unicode_escape')` when there is a `\\x`. Use it at priority 0 without the `_ascii` gate.\n- The day-9 solver's post-step (dead code, because lib had already unescaped): `if dec and \"\\\\u\" in dec or (dec and dec.lstrip().startswith('\"')): dec = json.loads(dec) if dec.strip().startswith('\"') else json.loads('\"' + dec + '\"')`\n\n(b) Answer conventions confirmed by the Game Master: slug only, `trim` normalization, accepted exactly as decoded. That is 45 of 45 for day 9 (Single, Time Trial and 43 Mastery sets), with no incorrect submissions. Mastery ids are `setN.message`, questions name `blob-NN.txt`, and the bundle is one zip saved as `blob-01.txt` (also the case on days 7-9).","usage":{"total_tokens":73098,"tool_uses":20,"duration_ms":158776},"uuid":"f33a9725-7d7b-49cc-974f-44c88086f141","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe"}
