{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DNdpbiFULwYVodx3YuqhwW","type":"tool_result","content":"72:\n73:## Day by day\n74:**Day 1 — You Must Be This Hash to Ride** (identity inventory). One text member (TT `roster.csv`, Mastery a renamed\n75:`evidence-note-copy.txt` + original). filename / size-bytes / md5 / sha1 / sha256 via `zipfile` + `hashlib`; CORRECT\n76:~36 s first try. Mastery zip-of-zips first seen.\n77:\n78:**Day 2 — Looks Can Be Deceiving** (magic prefix vs extension). Field `<member>-magic-prefix-hex-16`.\n79:- Answer = first 16 bytes of the member, lowercase hex, 32 chars, no `0x`/spaces. Single member was honest text.\n80:- Variants: TT `readme.exe` that was actually UTF-8 text; Mastery set2 `disguised-report.bin` that was a PDF.\n81:- TT quirk: contract question text named `roster.csv` while `answer_ids` said `readme-executable-...` and the zip held\n82:  only `readme.exe` -> fix was `lib.common.find_artifact_hinted` (match member to answer-id stem, exe~executable). Always\n83:  answer under `answer_ids`, trust the zip contents.\n84:- TT submits all came back `expired` (5 s window, harness latency, pre-Homebase) — not an analysis error.\n85:- Mastery zip-of-zips broke name lookup (outer zip has set1's name but not the member) -> returned the inner zip's\n86:  `PK..` bytes. Fix: `find_artifact` recurses nested zips (depth 4), prefers member whose parent zip is the named one.\n87:- Single CORRECT in ~34 s.\n88:\n89:**Day 3 — BOM Voyage** (`text.utf8_bom_present` enum `true`/`false`). First 3 bytes == `EF BB BF`; CORRECT ~28 s.\n90:Mastery `export-001-with-bom.txt` really had a BOM -- decide from bytes, never the name. utf16/32 variants unconfirmed.\n91:\n92:**Day 4 — Picture This** (JPEG). `jpeg.sof_dimensions_pixels` exact_text.\n93:- Walk segments by declared length (no fixed offsets) to the SOFn frame header; one SOF0 at 0x88; P=8, H, W.\n94:- GM-confirmed form `<width>x<height>` (X first, lowercase x, no spaces). Not EXIF/filename dims.\n95:- Prompt hinted rotation/\"presentation vs structure\" mismatch — not asked; solver carries best-effort exif_orientation /\n96:  display dims (unconfirmed). CORRECT ~38 s. TT/Mastery CORRECT in-window (solve phase 0.12 s of a 6 s window).\n97:\n98:**Day 5 — Chunk Norris** (`png.ihdr_dimensions_pixels`). IHDR @0x10 BE u32 width,height -> `<width>x<height>` (Day 4\n99:form by analogy, accepted). IDAT/CRC/after-IEND \"passenger\" checks were diagnostics only. CORRECT ~33 s, first try.\n100:\n101:**Day 6 — Portable Deception** (PDF). `pdf.header_version` exact_text.\n102:- `xxd -l 16` -> `%PDF-1.4` -> answer bare `x.y`. Only one `%PDF-` marker; no catalog `/Version`; exiftool PDFVersion agreed.\n103:- Rules adopted: header must be at file start (BOM/whitespace prefix tolerated); `%PDF-` deeper in the file (decoy in an\n104:  impostor) is NOT the header -> `none`; catalog `/Version` (PDF 32000 §7.2.2, incl. incremental updates) never changes\n105:  header_version. The impostor/`none` and override cases are synthetic (built by the worker), NOT GM-judged yet.\n106:- Mastery delivery changed: two downloads with the SAME filename, saved/addressed as `delivery 1: <zip>` /\n107:  `delivery 2: <zip>`; artifact field `delivery N: metadata-day-06-evidence.zip -> document-00N.pdf`.\n108:- Pre-fetched mastery contract.json listed document-003/004; the live attempt asked 006/007 -> read the live start.\n109:- CORRECT ~34 s; TT in_window 2.7 s (GM start call itself took 23 s that day — latency is outside the window).\n110:\n111:**Day 7 — Seven-Zip, No Relation** (ZIP EOCD census). `zip.eocd_total_entries` integer, id `d07-zip-001-zip-eocd-total-entries`.\n112:- Evidence zip held `evidence-drop-001.zip` (410 B, Stored, data-descriptor flag) with `room-01/item-1.txt`,\n113:  `room-02/item-1.txt` (identical 48 B text). EOCD total-entries u16 @+10 = 2 -> answer `2` (base-10, no units).\n114:- All variants were honest: EOCD disk/total == CD headers == LFHs, no comment/trailing bytes. The prompt's \"empty space\"\n115:  / \"census that does not add up\" (claim vs real walk, padding, dir entries) was flavor only — not exercised, so it is\n116:  still unknown whether the GM wants the claimed or the walked count when they differ. Answer the field = the CLAIM.\n117:- Worker: `xxd | tail` + `7z l -slt` on triage's pre-extracted inner zip, then stdlib `struct` EOCD parser in solve.py\n118:  (ZIP64 aware). CORRECT 57 s after start, first try. TT 3 entries (in_window 0.89 s / 7 s); Mastery set1 4, set2 5\n119:  (1.33 s / 7 s). Pre-fetched mastery contract (003/004) matched live this time.\n120:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015GTSiXQiFz2SK1f3Jnj6gx","agent_id":"aacda09a92d161c5d","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"4c7f29b3-cc70-41be-bf6a-0e948a4708b7","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:05:44.509Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DNdpbiFULwYVodx3YuqhwW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"metadata day09 technique log"}
