{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Kt5kSpcCKR7ahk3WVrRbVy","type":"tool_result","content":"72\t**D1 \"ELF Aware\"** (9 Qs; ~14 min of submits, 4 wrong). One plain C ELF64 x86-64 EXEC, not stripped. Fields: class, endianness,\n73\tmachine, e_type, `.huntress` marker (NUL-terminated string), has_symtab, exported (designated) symbol, recover_code constant, entry point.\n74\t- Tools: readelf -h/-S/-x, objdump (`mov $imm,%eax; ret`), pyelftools + capstone in the solver.\n75\t- Spelling laws learned the hard way: `ELF64` (not ELFCLASS64), `ET_EXEC` (not EXEC), `x86-64` (not EM_X86_64), `little` (not \"little endian\").\n76\t  The local wrong-answer cap (3 at the time) was hit on machine/endianness and needed operator probing.\n77\t- TT variants: 4-member \"slot\" bundle (`slot-0.elf`..`slot-3.elf`) with 36 answer ids `slotN_<qid>` → match ids to members by slot number.\n78\t  Profiles: stripped (has_symtab=false), \"section-beacon\" (designated fn renamed `inspect_section`; recover_code format turned\n79\t  exact_text with `none` allowed; submitting the renamed fn's constant was WRONG → `none` derived, still unconfirmed).\n80\t\n81\t**D2 \"Mangled\"** (17 Qs; ~22 min, 5 wrong). Zip = `day01-c.elf` + C++ build (`day02-cpp.elf`, or MinGW PE32+ `.exe` in variants).\n82\t- C++ config in section `.hcfg` = HCFG blob (first sighting). Decode: key=b[5], len=b[6]|b[7]<<8, plain=b[12+i]^key, verify crc32.\n83\t- Symbols: `mangled_score_symbol` = the mangled `<Class>::score` (`_ZNK..5scoreEPKc`), `vtable_symbol` = `_ZTV<class owning score>`\n84\t  (an unused base class has only _ZTI/_ZTS, no _ZTV → not the answer). Answer the MANGLED form, not the demangled one.\n85\t- `cpp_format`: ELF, ELF64, HCFG, elf64-x86-64, json all rejected → `elf`.\n86\t- PE sets kept failing in Mastery for hours: pe, exe, pe32+, coff, mz, elf were \"refuted\" one by one. Root cause: a set POST is\n87\t  all-or-nothing, and the real errors were the PE SYMBOL fields. For PE/COFF the GM wants the COMDAT section-name form\n88\t  `.text$<mangled>` (functions) / `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable/typeinfo). With those fixed, `pe` was accepted.\n89\t- Pitfall: the mutex `Global\\HuntressBR02_NNN` was sent with a doubled backslash (shell quoting), so the whole first batch failed.\n90\t\n91\t**D3 \"Table Manners\"** (24 Qs; ~1 h 48 min, ~60 wrong, the costliest binary day). Cumulative: d01 C ELF, d02 C++ ELF (same bytes as D2,\n92\tso the D2 answers carried over after a sha256 match), d03 .NET 8 PE32 i386 dll.\n93\t- .NET: `dnfile` gave the BSJB metadata version (`metadata_version` = root version string, e.g. v4.0.30319) and the FieldRVA blob;\n94\t  the `Campaign()` IL confirmed the HCFG layout. machine `i386` (x86 REJECTED for PE 0x14c).\n95\t- New d01 JSON fields: section_names = pyelftools `iter_sections()` names INCLUDING the leading \"\" NULL section; symbols = non-empty\n96\t  .symtab names in table order, dupes kept; disassembly = recover_code as capstone intel `\"{mnemonic} {op_str}\"` with DECIMAL immediates.\n97\t  Rejected disassembly forms: hex immediates, `\"ret \"` (trailing space from empty op_str), no space after comma, AT&T, main, whole .text, _start..hlt.\n98\t- `d03_analysis_format` = `pe_cli` (container + ECMA-335 CLI runtime). It took ~50 rejected synonyms first (pe, dotnet, .net, cil,\n99\t  msil, clr, managed, assembly, bsjb, dotnet_pe, ...). Worker spent 73 turns / 13.6 min plus operator probing. Lesson: compose labels from spec tokens.\n100\t\n101\t**D4 \"Go Fish\"** (32 Qs; ~1.5 min, 1 wrong). New d04 = static, stripped Go ELF (go1.25 buildinfo). Reused the D3 solver unchanged for d01-d03."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015GJR5XAWSfJ73EZEbfJaH3","agent_id":"a2870b1e01c4914ef","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"15c6d5d3-fb1c-4186-bc80-2132b71a1e2b","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:06:23.543Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Kt5kSpcCKR7ahk3WVrRbVy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","sourc