{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FnH16wBTFLsrQ9RNSRrPPL","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t- The D6 question text was REWRITTEN for formerly ambiguous fields: d01 disassembly now says \"Intel or AT&T spelling accepted\";\n101\t  d03 format says \"one container_runtime token; CLI, CLR or .NET accepted; separators/case accepted\". Read each question's full text and `syntax`.\n102\t\n103\t**D7 \"Routine Check\"** (56 Qs; 3 min start→CORRECT, 1 POST, 0 wrong). New d07 = `d07--variant-000.jar`, a 5 MB Kotlin fat jar\n104\t(Main-Class `Day07Variant000`, class major 65, ~3300 entries incl. the kotlin/ runtime). d01-d06 bytes identical to D6 (sha256 match).\n105\t- `javap -v -p Day07Variant000.class` → `private static final String CONFIG` ConstantValue base64 → HCFG (ver 1, key 0x31, len 368,\n106\t  crc32 checked). Answers: format `jar` (again), config values verbatim, hcfg_version `1`. Copied the D6 solver; only change: jar\n107\t  scan visits the Main-Class first and runtime packages last, returning at the first valid HCFG (D6 code scanned every class).\n108\t- Unasked \"state machine\": `staged$1 extends ContinuationImpl {int label; Object L$0}`; `main` reads env `HUNTRESS_HOST_MODEL`\n109\t  (default `workstation`) → `evaluate()` lookupswitch: workstation→`success`/13 events, analysis→`decoy`/7, sandbox→`failure`/3,\n110\t  else `failure`/1; prints trace JSON `huntress.binary.dynamic_trace.v1` {branch, event_count, campaign, family\n111\t  `loopback_stage_transfer`}. If branch/event questions appear: read them statically from `javap -c`, never run the jar.\n112\t- TT 5.8 s of an 11 s window, Mastery 6.4 s of 12 s, both first-try CORRECT (set2 had d02/d04 as PE `.exe`).\n113\t\n114\t**D8 \"Swift Justice\"** (80 Qs). New d08 = 67 MB static Swift ELF (~290k symbols, not stripped); old groups backfilled to 10 ids.\n115\t- **Read `answer_format.kind` first:** d08 elf_class/machine were `integer` → bit width `64` (not EI_CLASS `2`