teger).\n133\t- Lost time: one jq call selected `.answer_id` (null); contract questions use `.id`.\n134\t- TT 10 s window: 6.95 s in-window (download 3.45, solve 2.92), CORRECT first try. Mastery 20 s window, 5 sets / 450 ids:\n135\t  12.87 s in-window (download 6.62, solve 5.38), CORRECT first try.\n136\t\n137\t## GM answer conventions learned\n138\t| Field family | Accepted form | Rejected (never resubmit) |\n139\t|---|---|---|\n140\t| elf_class (`answer_format.kind` exact_text) | `ELF64` / `ELF32` (readelf style) | ELFCLASS64 |\n141\t| elf_class (`kind: integer`, D8 `d08_analysis_elf_class`) | the bit width `64` / `32` (single, TT, Mastery x5) | `2` / `1` (raw EI_CLASS byte; GM-rejected D8) |\n142\t| machine (`kind: integer`, D8 `d08_analysis_machine`) | decimal e_machine (`62` = x86-64; read u16 at offset 18 in EI_DATA order) | — |\n143\t| endianness | `little` / `big` | little endian, lsb, msb |\n144\t| machine (ELF) | `x86-64`, `x86`, `AArch64`, `ARM` | EM_X86_64, x86_64, amd64 |\n145\t| machine (PE FILE_HEADER) | 0x14c → `i386`; 0x8664 → `x86-64` | x86 (for PE i386); raw `0x8664` |\n146\t| architecture | the same machine words (Go ELF amd64 → `x86-64`; Go PE `.exe` 0x8664 → `x86-64`) | amd64, arm64, 386, x86_64 |\n147\t| elf_type | the constant `ET_EXEC` / `ET_DYN` | EXEC |\n148\t| entry_point, crc32_hex, xor_key_hex | lowercase hex with `0x` (crc `0x%08x`, key `0x%02x`) | — |\n149\t| recover_code | base-10 integer (`mov eax, 0x1fa4` → 8100); `none` if the named function is absent and the format allows it (inferred) | the renamed function's constant |\n150\t| has_symtab / has_cpp_* | enum `true`/`false` | — |\n151\t| marker | exact `.huntress` string without the NUL; `none` if the section is missing | — |\n152\t| format (native) | lowercase container: `elf`, `pe` (`macho` presumed) | ELF, ELF64, elf64-x86-64, HCFG, json, exe, pe32+, coff, mz |\n153\t| format (.NET) | `pe_cli` | ~50 synonyms (pe, pe32, dotnet, .net, cil, msil, clr, managed, assembly, ...) — lib/knowledge.py DOTNET_FORMAT_REJECTED |\n154\t| format (Java/Kotlin jar) | `jar` (D6 Java, D7 Kotlin) | jar_jvm |\n155\t| format / architecture (Swift D8, Nim D9 ELF) | `elf` / `x86-64`; D9 machine integer `62` (source language never changes the container label) | — |\n156\t| C++ symbols (ELF) | bare Itanium mangled name (`_ZNK...`, `_ZTV...`) | the demangled form |\n157\t| C++ symbols (PE/MinGW) | COMDAT section name `.text$<mangled>` (function), `.rdata$<mangled>` (vtable) | bare mangled name |\n158\t| section_names (JSON) | pyelftools order INCLUDING the leading `\"\"` | list without \"\" |\n159\t| symbols (JSON) | non-empty .symtab names, table order, dupes kept | list with the \"\" entries |\n160\t| disassembly (JSON) | capstone intel `\"mov eax, 8100\"`, `\"ret\"`, decimal immediates (D6 text says AT&T is also accepted) | hex imm, `\"ret \"`, `mov eax,0x..` |\n161\t| metadata_version | BSJB root string `v4.0.30319` | net8.0 / TFM / assembly version |\n162\t| config_* | values verbatim from the decoded HCFG JSON (mutex keeps ONE backslash) | JSON-escaped `\\\\` |\n163\t| hcfg_version | header byte 4 as a decimal integer | — |\n164\t| hcfg_offset (`kind: integer`, D9) | decimal FILE offset of the stored blob's first byte (base64 text start: `30696`), single+TT+Mastery x5 | — (not tried: VA 0x4077e8, struct 0x77e0, `strings -t d` 30695) |\n165\t| xor_key_hex | HCFG header byte 5 as `0x%02x` (D8: 0x51/0x61/0x71/0x31 for d04-d07) | — |\n166\t| compression_methods (jar, `kind: json`) | sorted distinct ZIP `compress_type` ids, compact: `[0,8]` | — |\n167\tNaming law (from playbook.py): native format = container only; a managed .NET binary = container_runtime from the spec tokens (pe+cli).\n168\tJava broke the compound law (`jar`), so when a label is new, try the plain container name AND the compound, one per POST.\n169\t\n170\t## Pitfalls that cost time\n171\t- **A multi-field POST is all-or-nothing.** One wrong field fails the set and hides which field was wrong. On D2 this made the correct `pe`\n172\t  look rejected for hours (the real error was the symbol form). Submit unconfirmed/new fields ALONE; batch only the known ones.\n173\t- **Guessing synonyms for a synthetic label** (D3 .NET format: ~50 tries, ~1.5 h). Derive from spec tokens and the playbook naming laws,\n174\t  use `hctf labels` (it ranks candidates from the playbook), and read the question `syntax` first: the GM has started embedding hints.\n175\t- **Shell/JSON quoting** of `Global\\Huntress...` mutexes: build the submit JSON with python/jq, not by hand in a shell string.\n176\t- **capstone `ret` has an empty op_str**: `f\"{m} {o}\"` gives `\"ret \"`. Strip it, and convert immediates to decimal.\n177\t- **Cumulative zip**: check whether the old groups' sha256 match a previous day's confirmed bytes. If yes, those answers carry over;\n178\t  spend the time on the NEW group only (D4-D6 took minutes because of this).\n179\t- **Recursive unzip** destroys nested containers (.jar/.apk) and their `dNN--` prefix; keep them whole.\n180\t- **Same field name, different `kind`** (D8 elf_class/machine): a solver keyed only on the field name emits `ELF64` for an integer\n181\t  question. Read `answer_format.kind` per id.\n182\t- **Huge members** (D8: 67 MB Swift static-stdlib ELF): any per-key xor brute force or per-field re-parse blows a 10 s window.\n183\t  Cheap encodings first (raw magic, base64 magic `SENGR`), crc-gate every hit, parse each member once.\n184\t- **Decoy magics** (D9 Nim): the code that CHECKS the magic embeds `\"HCFG\"` (and an assert message) as literals, so the first\n185\t  raw hit is not the blob. A decoder that returns on the first crc-\"valid\" hit (empty len 0 => crc32(b\"\")==0 passes!) stops\n186\t  early; require non-empty JSON that parses, then keep scanning, then try the base64 form.\n187\t- **`strings -t d` offsets on Nim/Swift literals**: the byte before the text can be printable (Nim's strlit flag 0x40 = `@`), so\n188\t  `strings` reports offset-1 (30695). Take offsets from `grep -abo`/`re.finditer(...).start()` on the exact token.\n189\t- **Jar members are deflated**: `grep HCFG file.jar` finds nothing. Inflate the class, read constant-pool strings, base64-decode.\n190\t  In a fat jar (Kotlin/Scala/shaded) scan the Main-Class first; a full scan of ~3000 runtime classes eats timed windows.\n191\t- **Stripped builds** in variants (D1 slot, D2 Mastery set2, D8 Mastery d01): no recover_code symbol. Answer what the question\n192\t  defines for absence (`[]` for the disassembly, `none` where allowed), has_symtab=false. The old leaf `mov eax, imm; ret` guess\n193\t  failed all 5 D8 Mastery sets.\n194\t- **Renamed designated function** (D1 TT section-beacon): the question still says recover_code. Answer `none` (when the format allows it), not the other function's constant.\n195\t- **Tool parity** (2026-10-07): ilspycmd, dotnet, rustfilt, GoReSym (`GoReSym -t -p file`), rabin2 are installed in\n196\t  `bin/`; monodis/de4dot are not (dnfile covers .NET metadata).\n197\t- **Timed windows are ~6-12 s**: D2 TT/Mastery attempts expired from download/orchestration latency, not solver speed (the solver ran in 0.3-0.5 s).\n198\t  After editing hctf/*.py, restart the orchestrator. D1/D2 runs used stale modules and kept sending only the slot0 ids.\n199\t- **PE machine map must include 0x8664 → `x86-64`**: a from-scratch replay once emitted `0x8664` and failed TT twice.\n200\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015GJR5XAWSfJ73EZEbfJaH3","agent_id":"a2870b1e01c4914ef","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"ccee1629-d5a5-4513-8aa7-2afba8c50aa9","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:06:43.778Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01FnH16wBTFLsrQ9RNSRrPPL","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"binary day09 technique log"}
