{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfriLTLtp3a7JKkfa1xFD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I updated `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/metadata-forensics.md`; it is now 210 lines. That is the only file I edited.\n\n**What I added**\n- **Header:** the title now says days 1-9. Day 9 extended the cumulative kit with a 1.26 MB `telemetry-agent-001.exe` and moved the lane into executable headers with `pe.coff_machine_u16_hex` (id family `d09-pe-001`). I also added a note that the flavor text promised more than the sample delivered: \"several architectures, plus decoys\" turned out to be one honest i386 PE in every mode.\n- **Day 9 entry:**\n  - **Artifact:** a Go 1.22.2 PE32 exe (`GOARCH=386`). e_lfanew is 0x80, Machine reads `0x014c`, and the optional-header magic is 0x10b.\n  - **How it was solved:** `xxd` plus a 3-line `struct` read (0x3C, then `PE\\0\\0`, then a little-endian u16). The worker copied the Day 8 solver and added one answer-id suffix branch.\n  - **Timing:** start 13:00:07.1Z to CORRECT 13:00:54.5Z, about 47 s, right first time with all 13 answers.\n  - **Time Trial:** 6 s window, used 2.88 s, of which the submit round-trip was 2.31 s. CORRECT.\n  - **Mastery:** 5 sets × 13 = 65 answers in a 7 s window, used 2.49 s, of which solving took 0.86 s. CORRECT.\n- **Variant axes:** the field set now goes up to 13 / 65. Machine was 0x014c in all 7 copies, but the exe bytes differ per set. `pattern` answers with `trim` are case-sensitive. New axis: TT and Mastery append ` [assigned-artifact-sha256:<hex>]` to the first question's text.\n- **Recognition cues:** new rows for walking a PE COFF header, for the ELF and Mach-O sibling fields (including fat binaries and the `cafebabe` clash with Java class files), and for `.exe` decoys (no `PE\\0\\0` at e_lfanew means `none`).\n- **Conventions:** a `_u16_hex` field is answered as `0x` plus 4 zero-padded lowercase hex digits (`0x014c`). It is not the binary lane's word `i386`, and not unpadded `0x14c`, which is untested.\n- **Delivery layouts:** the Mastery download is named `<challenge-id>-mastery.zip` while the questions reference `...-evidence-0N.zip`, so the bundle has to be found by sha256.\n- **Pitfalls:** windows have shrunk to 6/7 s. Big exe members need in-memory caching. Don't take the answer from `file`, `pefile` or GOARCH. The solver skeleton is not the previous day's solver. The pre-fetched `start_required` contract has `questions` but no `answer_ids`.\n- **Compression:** I shortened the Day 1-6 entries.\n\n**Candidate lib additions** (I did not edit anything under `lib/`)\n1. **`knowledge.py`:** add `PE_COFF_MACHINE_U16_HEX_FMT = \"0x{:04x}\"`. The GM confirmed `0x014c` in single, TT and all five Mastery sets (`*/confirmed.json`) with no wrong submissions. There is nothing for metadata hex-field formats in it now; `PE_MACHINE` maps to words only.\n2. **`playbook.py`:** add a lane rule saying a `<fmt>.<field>_uNN_hex` suffix means `0x` plus lowercase hex zero-padded to NN/4 digits. It should say this differs from the binary-lane `machine` rule (`0x14c` → `i386`), so the two are never mixed up.\n3. **New helper in `lib/binary.py`:** there is currently no PE header parser in lib. The Day 9 solver wrote its own:\n   ```python\n   def _pe_machine(d):\n       if d[:2] != b\"MZ\" or len(d) < 0x40: return \"none\"\n       o = struct.unpack_from(\"<I\", d, 0x3C)[0]\n       if o + 6 > len(d) or d[o:o+4] != b\"PE\\0\\0\": return \"none\"\n       return \"0x%04x\" % struct.unpack_from(\"<H\", d, o + 4)[0]\n   ```\n   It handles MZ-only and non-PE decoys by returning `none`. The solver also pre-armed an untested `elf-e-machine-u16-hex` branch (`\"0x%04x\"` of the u16 at offset 18, byte order from EI_DATA). A general `pe_coff_header(data)` returning machine, nsections, timestamp, optional-header magic and characteristics would cover future `pe.coff_*` fields.\n\nEvidence files are in `/home/testp