{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CfriMuYkWvEagJijHoWKb","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I added a Day 9 entry to `/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/techniques/binary-reverse-engineering.md` and revised the sections around it. The file is now 200 lines, and the only file I edited is that doc.\n\n**What changed in the doc**\n- **Title and overview:** the title now says days 1-9. The overview now covers the D9 Nim ELF, a field count of 90, and the base64 Nim string literal holding the config. It also notes that each day has added about one never-seen field, which was `hcfg_offset` on D9.\n- **Variant axes:**\n  - The HCFG scan rule now requires the JSON to parse and keeps scanning past a failed hit.\n  - New axis \"Location-as-answer\": `hcfg_offset` is the file offset of the stored blob's first byte. It was 30696 in all 6 variants, but should still be computed.\n  - D9 variant indices are recorded: TT matched Mastery set1 for d02-d09 but not d01, and Mastery d01 was the same build with `8104` in all 5 sets.\n  - Mastery had 5 sets again, with set2/set4 shipping d02/d04 as PE.\n  - New on D9 in every lane: the first question of each set ends with `Evidence case: d09-{tt,m}-<hex>. [assigned-artifact-sha256:<zip sha>]`, which maps each set to its download.\n- **Recognition cues:** new Nim row. Fingerprints are `NimMain`/`PreMain`, `TM__<hash>_N` literals, `proc__mod_uN` names and `@m..@snim@slib...nim.c` strings. The config proc returns `mov eax,len; lea rdx,[TM__]`, and the text starts 8 bytes in, after a cap word with flag 0x40.\n- **D9 entry:**\n  - 86 s from start to CORRECT, one POST, nothing rejected. The copied D8 solver already answered 89 of 90 ids.\n  - It records the exact grep/objdump commands and the two decoy `HCFG` hits.\n  - Time lost: one jq query used `.answer_id` instead of `.id`.\n  - Time Trial took 6.95 s of a 10 s window. Mastery took 12.87 s of a 20 s window (5 sets, 450 ids). Both were correct on the first try.\n- **Day 8:** the stray heading is now a bold entry under Day by day. I shortened D1-D3 so the file stays near 200 lines.\n- **Conventions table:** added the `hcfg_offset` row and folded the D9 `elf`/`x86-64`/`62` answers into the existing Swift row.\n- **Pitfalls:** two new ones.\n  - Decoy magic: a length-0 header passes the CRC32 check, so the first raw hit stops a naive decoder.\n  - `strings -t d` reports Nim literal offsets one byte early (the `@` is the flag byte).\n\n**Candidate lib additions**\n1. `knowledge.py` doesn't have `hcfg_offset` yet. The GM accepted it in single solve, Time Trial and all 5 Mastery sets. Suggested entry: `HCFG_OFFSET_FMT = \"{n}\"`, the decimal file offset of the stored blob's first byte (the base64 text start, 30696 = 0x77e8; not the VA 0x4077e8 or the literal header at 0x77e0). The value for a raw-blob member is unconfirmed.\n2. The playbook could gain a rule: questions may carry `[assigned-artifact-sha256:<sha>]`, which maps each set to its delivery. That tag is question text and never part of an answer. I saw it in every D9 lane's Time Trial/Mastery contract.\n3. Lib has no HCFG decoder at all; each solver carries its own `hcfg`/`native_hcfg`. The D9 solver's only new branch was in `native_hcfg`, recording the offset of the validated base64 match:\n   ```python\n   if h and h[\"config\"] is not None:\n       h[\"offset\"] = m.start()   # Day 9 Nim: file offset of the base64 string literal\n       return h\n   ```\n   I'd propose a `lib.binary.hcfg_find(data)` that returns `{offset, encoding: raw|b64|hex, key, version, crc, config}`. It should skip hits whose JSON is empty or doesn't parse rather than returning on the first one: the solver's `hcfg()` currently stops at the length-0 Nim decoy. It should also set the offset on the raw and hex paths, which the solver leaves out.\n\nNo new `lib/elf.py` branch was needed; `fields()` already covers the integer machine answer (`62`)."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":377,"cache_read_input_tokens":119164,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":377,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":835,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_015GJR5XAWSfJ73EZEbfJaH3","agent_id":"a2870b1e01c4914ef","session_id":"1b2a5880-b146-4584-b0b5-a8899fa1bffe","uuid":"34cdf2bb-958b-452b-9cfc-706f30ba0097","timestamp":"2026-10-09T13:07:12.627Z","request_id":"req_011CfriMu9wXrbqKeHe2vqpM","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"binary day09 technique log"}
